@startuml

title 07. Payments

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

enum PaymentDirection {
	incoming
	outgoing
}

enum PaymentType {
	cash
	card
	bank_transfer
	online
	refund
	other
}

enum PaymentStatusEnum {
	unpaid
	partially_paid
	paid
	overpaid
	refunded
}

entity Payment {
	* id: int
	--
	* direction: PaymentDirection
	* type: PaymentType
	* amount: decimal(14,4)
	* amountBase: decimal(14,4)
	* paidAt: DateTimeImmutable
	comment: text?
	externalReference: string(255)?
	* currency: Currency
	* exchangeRateToBase: decimal(18,8)
	* store: Store
	order: Order?
	purchase: Purchase?
	reversesPayment: Payment?
	createdBy: User?
	updatedBy: User?
	* createdAt: DateTimeImmutable
	* updatedAt: DateTimeImmutable
}

Store ||--o{ Payment : has payments
Currency ||--o{ Payment : payment currency
Order |o--o{ Payment : paid by
Purchase |o--o{ Payment : paid by
Payment |o--o| Payment : reversal of
PaymentDirection ||--o{ Payment : defines
PaymentType ||--o{ Payment : classifies
PaymentStatusEnum ||--o{ Order : payment state
PaymentStatusEnum ||--o{ Purchase : payment state
User |o--o{ Payment : records/updates

note right of Payment
  Current project status:
  - Payment entity is implemented.
  - PaymentDirection and PaymentType are implemented.
  - PaymentStatusEnum already exists because Order/Purchase use it.
  - Order/Purchase have paidAmountBase/paymentStatus/paidAt cache fields,
    maintained by PaymentRecalculationService.

  Required behavior:
  - Exactly one of order or purchase is filled.
  - Incoming payments usually apply to Order.
  - Outgoing payments usually apply to Purchase.
  - Refunds are explicit payment rows, never direct edits to totals.
  - Corrections use linked reversal rows; recorded payments are not edited.
  - Every reversal requires an explicit business reason on the refund row.
  - amount is in payment currency; amountBase uses exchangeRate snapshot.
  - Payment rows are the financial source of truth.
  - Order/Purchase payment fields are denormalized caches.
end note

note right of PaymentStatusEnum
  Derived state for Order/Purchase:
  - unpaid: paidAmountBase = 0.
  - partially_paid: 0 < paidAmountBase < totalAmountBase.
  - paid: paidAmountBase = totalAmountBase.
  - overpaid: paidAmountBase > totalAmountBase.
  - refunded: effective paid amount returned to 0 after refund,
    when business rules need a distinct visible state.
end note

note bottom
  Suggested implementation steps:

  1. Add Payment entity, enums, repository and manager.
  2. Add Payment CRUD scoped by Store.
  3. Add payment sections to Order show and Purchase show.
  4. Add PaymentRecalculationService:
     - recalculate paidAmountBase
     - recalculate paymentStatus
     - set paidAt when a document first becomes fully paid.
  5. Recalculate after create and explicit reversal corrections.
  6. Add tests for relation exclusivity, exchange-rate snapshots,
     unpaid/partial/paid/overpaid/refunded states and refunds.

  Do this after Order/Purchase base CRUD exists.
end note

@enduml
